# Tests for the Ptc_family module (Form 8962 lines 1 to 8)

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with the concrete cases of issue #32,
worked out by hand from the Instructions for Form 8962 (2024)
(`sources/forms-instructions/i8962--2024.pdf`: Tables 1-1 to 1-3 p 8,
Worksheet 2 p 9, Table 2 p 10, lines 8a and 8b p 11). Table 2 in full is in
`catala/tests/test_ptc_table2.catala_en`. Oracle comparison:
`make difftest SCOPE=ptc_family`.

> Using Types
> Using Ptc_family as F

## Helper: a return with defaults

By default: a single filer in the 48 states, no dependents, nobody can claim
the filer, AGI $0, no tax-exempt interest, no nontaxable Social Security.
A test overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context dependents content integer
  context primary_claimable condition
  context secondary_claimable condition
  context alaska condition
  context hawaii condition
  context agi content money
  context exempt_interest content money
  context nontaxable_ss content money
  f scope F.PtcFamily
  output family_size content integer
  output poverty_line content money
  output magi content money
  output income content money
  output percent content decimal
  output figure content decimal
  output annual content money
  output monthly content money

scope Case:
  definition filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition dependents equals 0
  definition primary_claimable equals false
  definition secondary_claimable equals false
  definition alaska equals false
  definition hawaii equals false
  definition agi equals $0
  definition exempt_interest equals $0
  definition nontaxable_ss equals $0

  definition f.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition f.claimed_dependents_count equals dependents
  definition f.primary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals primary_claimable
  definition f.secondary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals secondary_claimable
  definition f.lived_in_ak equals alaska
  definition f.lived_in_hi equals hawaii
  definition f.agi equals agi
  definition f.tax_exempt_interest equals exempt_interest
  definition f.non_taxable_social_security_benefits equals nontaxable_ss

  definition family_size equals f.tax_family_size
  definition poverty_line equals f.federal_poverty_level_threshold
  definition magi equals f.ptc_magi
  definition income equals f.household_income
  definition percent equals f.household_income_as_percent
  definition figure equals f.applicable_figure
  definition annual equals f.ptc_annual_contribution_amount
  definition monthly equals f.ptc_monthly_contribution_amount
```

## Tax family size (line 1)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingleFamilySizeOne:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingleFamilySizeOne:
  assertion c.family_size = 1
  assertion c.family_size != 2
  assertion c.poverty_line = $14,580
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjWithOneChildFamilySizeThree:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjWithOneChildFamilySizeThree:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.dependents equals 1
  assertion c.family_size = 3
  assertion c.poverty_line = $24,860
  assertion c.poverty_line != $19,720
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHohWithTwoChildrenFamilySizeThree:
  c scope Case

scope TestHohWithTwoChildrenFamilySizeThree:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition c.dependents equals 2
  assertion c.family_size = 3
  assertion c.poverty_line = $24,860
```

A filer who can be claimed as a dependent is not in their own tax family
(instructions for line 1, p 7).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestClaimableFilerIsNotCounted:
  c scope Case

scope TestClaimableFilerIsNotCounted:
  definition c.primary_claimable equals true
  assertion c.family_size = 0
  assertion c.poverty_line = $0
  assertion c.percent = 0.0
  assertion c.annual = $0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjOneSpouseClaimable:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjOneSpouseClaimable:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.secondary_claimable equals true
  assertion c.family_size = 1
```

## Federal poverty line (line 4), Tables 1-1 to 1-3

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPovertyLineTable11:
  c1 scope Case
  c2 scope Case
  c4 scope Case
  c5 scope Case
  c8 scope Case
  c11 scope Case

scope TestPovertyLineTable11:
  definition c2.dependents equals 1
  definition c4.dependents equals 3
  definition c5.dependents equals 4
  definition c8.dependents equals 7
  definition c11.dependents equals 10
  assertion c1.poverty_line = $14,580
  assertion c2.poverty_line = $19,720
  assertion c4.poverty_line = $30,000
  assertion c5.poverty_line = $35,140
  assertion c8.poverty_line = $50,560
  assertion c11.family_size = 11
  # "Multiply $5,140 by 3 and add the result of $15,420 to $50,560. Enter the
  # result of $65,980" (i8962 p 8)
  assertion c11.poverty_line = $65,980
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPovertyLineAlaska:
  c1 scope Case
  c3 scope Case
  c11 scope Case

scope TestPovertyLineAlaska:
  definition c1.alaska equals true
  definition c3.alaska equals true
  definition c3.dependents equals 2
  definition c11.alaska equals true
  definition c11.dependents equals 10
  assertion c1.poverty_line = $18,210
  assertion c3.poverty_line = $31,070
  # Table 1-2 note: $82,510 for 11 people
  assertion c11.poverty_line = $82,510
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPovertyLineHawaii:
  c1 scope Case
  c3 scope Case
  c11 scope Case

scope TestPovertyLineHawaii:
  definition c1.hawaii equals true
  definition c3.hawaii equals true
  definition c3.dependents equals 2
  definition c11.hawaii equals true
  definition c11.dependents equals 10
  assertion c1.poverty_line = $16,770
  assertion c3.poverty_line = $28,590
  # Table 1-3 note: $75,870 for 11 people
  assertion c11.poverty_line = $75,870
```

## Household income (lines 2a and 3)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestModifiedAgiAddsInterestAndSocialSecurity:
  c scope Case

scope TestModifiedAgiAddsInterestAndSocialSecurity:
  definition c.agi equals $40,000
  definition c.exempt_interest equals $1,200
  definition c.nontaxable_ss equals $3,000
  assertion c.magi = $44,200
  assertion c.income = $44,200
  assertion c.income != $40,000
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNegativeMagiGivesZeroHouseholdIncome:
  c scope Case

scope TestNegativeMagiGivesZeroHouseholdIncome:
  definition c.agi equals -$300
  assertion c.magi = -$300
  assertion c.income = $0
  assertion c.percent = 0.0
  assertion c.annual = $0
```

## Household income as a percent of the line (line 5)

Single, 48 states, line $14,580 (so 1% is $145.80 and 4 times is $58,320).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestExactlyFourTimesIsFourHundred:
  c scope Case

scope TestExactlyFourTimesIsFourHundred:
  definition c.agi equals $58,320
  assertion c.percent = 400.0
  assertion c.percent != 401.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.085
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestJustAboveFourTimesIsFourHundredOne:
  c scope Case

scope TestJustAboveFourTimesIsFourHundredOne:
  definition c.agi equals $58,321
  assertion c.percent = 401.0
  assertion c.percent != 400.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.085
  assertion c.annual = $4,957
```

A percentage is truncated, never rounded: $14,579 over $14,580 is 99.99
percent, so 99, not 100 (Worksheet 2's examples: 0.9984 gives 99, 1.8565
gives 185, 3.997 gives 399).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPercentIsTruncatedNotRounded:
  just_below scope Case
  below_two scope Case
  below_four scope Case

scope TestPercentIsTruncatedNotRounded:
  definition just_below.agi equals $14,579
  definition below_two.agi equals $27,000
  definition below_four.agi equals $58,300
  assertion just_below.percent = 99.0
  assertion just_below.percent != 100.0
  assertion below_two.percent = 185.0
  assertion below_four.percent = 399.0
  assertion below_four.percent != 400.0
```

## Applicable figure (line 7) and contribution amount (lines 8a, 8b)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFigureAt150PercentIsZero:
  c scope Case

scope TestFigureAt150PercentIsZero:
  # 150 percent of $14,580 is exactly $21,870
  definition c.agi equals $21,870
  assertion c.percent = 150.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.0
  assertion c.annual = $0
  assertion c.monthly = $0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFigureAt300PercentIsSixPercent:
  c scope Case

scope TestFigureAt300PercentIsSixPercent:
  # 300 percent of $14,580 is exactly $43,740
  definition c.agi equals $43,740
  assertion c.percent = 300.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.06
  assertion c.figure != 0.0603
  # 43,740 * 0.06 = 2,624.40; 2,624 / 12 = 218.67
  assertion c.annual = $2,624
  assertion c.monthly = $219
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFigureAtFourHundredPercentIsEightAndAHalf:
  c scope Case

scope TestFigureAtFourHundredPercentIsEightAndAHalf:
  definition c.agi equals $58,320
  assertion c.figure = 0.085
  # 58,320 * 0.085 = 4,957.20
  assertion c.annual = $4,957
  assertion c.monthly = $413
```

Table 2 rows 301 and 399 (the half-up rounding of the 0.00025 steps).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFigureHalfUpRows:
  r301 scope Case
  r302 scope Case
  r399 scope Case

scope TestFigureHalfUpRows:
  # 301% of 14,580 = 43,885.80, so $43,886 gives 301.01...: 301
  definition r301.agi equals $43,886
  definition r302.agi equals $44,032
  definition r399.agi equals $58,175
  assertion r301.percent = 301.0
  assertion r301.figure = 0.0603
  assertion r302.percent = 302.0
  assertion r302.figure = 0.0605
  assertion r399.percent = 399.0
  assertion r399.figure = 0.0848
  assertion r301.figure != 0.0602
```

A product that is not a whole dollar is rounded once: 45,100 * 0.0623 =
2,809.73, so 2,810 (oracle scenario `ptc-annual-amounts-rounding`: 309
percent, 2,810, monthly 234). The $1,115.4958 case of the DF comment rounds to
$1,115, not $1,116.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAnnualContributionRoundsOnce:
  c scope Case

scope TestAnnualContributionRoundsOnce:
  definition c.agi equals $45,100
  assertion c.percent = 309.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.0623
  assertion c.annual = $2,810
  assertion c.monthly = $234
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFigureMiddleRows:
  r151 scope Case
  r200 scope Case
  r250 scope Case

scope TestFigureMiddleRows:
  # 151 percent: ceiling(151 * 145.80) = 22,016
  definition r151.agi equals $22,016
  # 200 percent: 29,160; 250 percent: 36,450
  definition r200.agi equals $29,160
  definition r250.agi equals $36,450
  assertion r151.percent = 151.0
  assertion r151.figure = 0.0004
  assertion r200.figure = 0.02
  assertion r250.figure = 0.04
  assertion r200.annual = $583
```

A two-person joint return uses $19,720 (150 percent is $29,580).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjUsesFamilyOfTwoLine:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjUsesFamilyOfTwoLine:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $50,000
  assertion c.poverty_line = $19,720
  assertion c.percent = 253.0
  assertion c.figure = 0.0412
  assertion c.annual = $2,060
  assertion c.monthly = $172
```

## Bad outputs are rejected

The percentage 99.99 is never entered as 100, and a household income of
exactly 4 times the line is never entered as 401.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBadOutputsRejected:
  c scope Case
  d scope Case

scope TestBadOutputsRejected:
  definition c.agi equals $14,579
  definition d.agi equals $58,320
  assertion not (c.percent = 100.0)
  assertion not (d.percent = 401.0)
  assertion not (d.figure = 0.0)
```
